{"3940090": {"success": true, "data": {"type": "game", "name": "Atrium Mortis", "steam_appid": 3940090, "required_age": 0, "is_free": false, "detailed_description": "<p class=\"bb_paragraph\" ><i>One wrong door, and the Atrium will swallow you whole.</i></p><p class=\"bb_paragraph\" >You awaken in an ancient Roman hall that loops forever. The only way out is to identify what doesn’t belong. Statues turning to face you, banners changing colour, footsteps behind you - anything could be the clue. Choose wrong, and you’re cast back to Hall 0. Choose right, and the Atrium lets you progress.</p><p class=\"bb_paragraph\" >But it's not as easy as just spotting anomalies. Sometimes, the anomaly is obvious - the problem is <i>getting past it</i>.</p><h2 class=\"bb_tag\" ><strong>Face the Atrium’s Monsters</strong></h2><p class=\"bb_paragraph\" >The halls aren’t empty. Angels of death drift silently between the columns, their presence warping the air. Stranger things lurk beyond - entities you can’t yet name, but will come to fear. Some can be avoided… others demand confrontation.</p><h2 class=\"bb_tag\" ><strong>A Roguelite Puzzle of Observation and Nerve</strong></h2><ul class=\"bb_ul\"><li><p class=\"bb_paragraph\" ><strong>Spot the anomaly</strong> – Each corridor hides something amiss. A banner bleeding new colours. A statue’s eyes that follow you. A torch that burns too cold.</p></li><li><p class=\"bb_paragraph\" ><strong>Left or right</strong> – Anomaly detected? Take the left door. Nothing wrong? Take the right. But beware: the Atrium has a way of warping your perception.</p></li><li><p class=\"bb_paragraph\" ><strong>Puzzles in your path</strong> – Sometimes the left door won’t open until you solve a challenge; locate a hidden key, decipher an inscription, or answer a cryptic riddle.</p></li><li><p class=\"bb_paragraph\" ><strong>Lurking Terrors</strong> – Angels of Death and nightmarish beings haunt the halls, punishing the slightest mistake.</p></li><li><p class=\"bb_paragraph\" ><strong>Grow Stronger with Every Run - </strong>Your journey is never wasted. Earn diamonds to unlock permanent upgrades. Like <i>Hindsight</i> to review missed anomalies, <i>Foresight</i> to glimpse anomaly odds, or a <i>Radiant Sword</i> to strike down Angels of Death.</p></li><li><p class=\"bb_paragraph\" ><strong>Conquer the Final Trial - </strong>Hall 10 holds the Atrium’s ultimate guardian. Only the strongest souls will survive what waits there.</p></li><li><p class=\"bb_paragraph\" ><strong>Optional Jumpscares -</strong> Too scared? Turn them off in settings.</p></li></ul>", "about_the_game": "<p class=\"bb_paragraph\" ><i>One wrong door, and the Atrium will swallow you whole.</i></p><p class=\"bb_paragraph\" >You awaken in an ancient Roman hall that loops forever. The only way out is to identify what doesn’t belong. Statues turning to face you, banners changing colour, footsteps behind you - anything could be the clue. Choose wrong, and you’re cast back to Hall 0. Choose right, and the Atrium lets you progress.</p><p class=\"bb_paragraph\" >But it's not as easy as just spotting anomalies. Sometimes, the anomaly is obvious - the problem is <i>getting past it</i>.</p><h2 class=\"bb_tag\" ><strong>Face the Atrium’s Monsters</strong></h2><p class=\"bb_paragraph\" >The halls aren’t empty. Angels of death drift silently between the columns, their presence warping the air. Stranger things lurk beyond - entities you can’t yet name, but will come to fear. Some can be avoided… others demand confrontation.</p><h2 class=\"bb_tag\" ><strong>A Roguelite Puzzle of Observation and Nerve</strong></h2><ul class=\"bb_ul\"><li><p class=\"bb_paragraph\" ><strong>Spot the anomaly</strong> – Each corridor hides something amiss. A banner bleeding new colours. A statue’s eyes that follow you. A torch that burns too cold.</p></li><li><p class=\"bb_paragraph\" ><strong>Left or right</strong> – Anomaly detected? Take the left door. Nothing wrong? Take the right. But beware: the Atrium has a way of warping your perception.</p></li><li><p class=\"bb_paragraph\" ><strong>Puzzles in your path</strong> – Sometimes the left door won’t open until you solve a challenge; locate a hidden key, decipher an inscription, or answer a cryptic riddle.</p></li><li><p class=\"bb_paragraph\" ><strong>Lurking Terrors</strong> – Angels of Death and nightmarish beings haunt the halls, punishing the slightest mistake.</p></li><li><p class=\"bb_paragraph\" ><strong>Grow Stronger with Every Run - </strong>Your journey is never wasted. Earn diamonds to unlock permanent upgrades. Like <i>Hindsight</i> to review missed anomalies, <i>Foresight</i> to glimpse anomaly odds, or a <i>Radiant Sword</i> to strike down Angels of Death.</p></li><li><p class=\"bb_paragraph\" ><strong>Conquer the Final Trial - </strong>Hall 10 holds the Atrium’s ultimate guardian. Only the strongest souls will survive what waits there.</p></li><li><p class=\"bb_paragraph\" ><strong>Optional Jumpscares -</strong> Too scared? Turn them off in settings.</p></li></ul>", "short_description": "Trapped in an endless Roman corridor, you must observe carefully, solve eerie puzzles, and survive horrors in this roguelite puzzle-adventure.", "supported_languages": "English<strong>*</strong>, French<strong>*</strong>, Italian<strong>*</strong>, German<strong>*</strong>, Spanish - Spain<strong>*</strong>, Japanese<strong>*</strong>, Korean<strong>*</strong>, Portuguese - Brazil<strong>*</strong>, Russian<strong>*</strong>, Simplified Chinese<strong>*</strong><br><strong>*</strong>languages with full audio support", "header_image": "https://shared.akamai.steamstatic.com/store_item_assets/steam/apps/3940090/863f73696948c948467bd28c6546586f4aba3d09/header.jpg?t=1769704978", "capsule_image": "https://shared.akamai.steamstatic.com/store_item_assets/steam/apps/3940090/c5025b6349eae8d5ad24c8dd36669d49ed1e269c/capsule_231x87.jpg?t=1769704978", "capsule_imagev5": "https://shared.akamai.steamstatic.com/store_it